The critical length beyond which trigger-wave propagation outpaces diffusion can be derived as follows. We approximate the elevated nuclear pool as a point source (valid in the far field, x ≫ RNucleus) diffusing into a cytoplasmic background CC, so that the concentration profile is
(10)
C(x,t)≈CC+(CN−CC)exp⁡(−x24Dt), \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{equation*} C(x, t) \approx C_{\mathrm{C}}+\left(C_{\mathrm{N}}-C_{\mathrm{C}}\right) \exp \left(-\frac{x^{2}}{4 D t}\right), \tag{10} \end{equation*}$$\end{document}
where CN is the initial nuclear concentration. Requiring the concentration to reach the excitation threshold CTh, we solve C(x, t) = CTh for the threshold-crossing position,
(11)
x(t)≈4Dtln⁡(CN−CCCTh−CC). \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{equation*} x(t) \approx \sqrt{4 D t \ln \left(\frac{C_{\mathrm{N}}-C_{\mathrm{C}}}{C_{\mathrm{Th}}-C_{\mathrm{C}}}\right)} . \tag{11} \end{equation*}$$\end{document}
The speed at which this threshold crossing advances follows by differentiation,
(12)
vD(t)=dxdt=Dln⁡[(CN−CC)/(CTh−CC)]t, \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{equation*} v_{\mathrm{D}}(t)=\frac{d x}{d t}=\sqrt{\frac{D \ln \left[\left(C_{\mathrm{N}}-C_{\mathrm{C}}\right) /\left(C_{\mathrm{Th}}-C_{\mathrm{C}}\right)\right]}{t}}, \tag{12} \end{equation*}$$\end{document}
and decreases as t−1∕2. The trigger wave, by contrast, advances at the constant front velocity vF. Equating vF = vD defines the crossover time
(13)
CCrit=DvF2ln⁡(CN−CCCTh−CC), \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{equation*} \mathrm{C}_{\mathrm{Crit}}=\frac{D}{v_{\mathrm{F}}^{2}} \ln \left(\frac{C_{\mathrm{N}}-C_{\mathrm{C}}}{C_{\mathrm{Th}}-C_{\mathrm{C}}}\right), \tag{13} \end{equation*}$$\end{document}
and, using LCrit = vF tCrit, the critical length
(14)
LCrit=DvFln⁡(CN−CCCTh−CC), \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{equation*} L_{\mathrm{Crit}}=\frac{D}{v_{\mathrm{F}}} \ln \left(\frac{C_{\mathrm{N}}-C_{\mathrm{C}}}{C_{\mathrm{Th}}-C_{\mathrm{C}}}\right), \tag{14} \end{equation*}$$\end{document}
which is the expression quoted in the main text (with C ≡ [Cyclin B-Cdk1]). Below LCrit the front is diffusion-limited; above it, propagation proceeds at the constant trigger-wave speed vF.
